  "priorExpiration": "2008-10-19",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-M 203.10 Civil Action. Any party aggrieved by the findings and decisions of the appointed impartial person in the due process proceedings as set out in He-M 203.03 through He-M 203.08 may immediately bring a civil action in state or federal court under § 639 (a) (1) of the IDEIA.\n\nSource. #5744, eff 12-1-93; ss by #6727, eff 4-1-98; ss by #7233, eff 4-22-00; ss by #9135, INTERIM, eff 4-22-08, EXPIRED: 10-19-08\n\nNew. #9593, eff 11-11-09 (from He-M 203.07); ss by #10324, eff 4-26-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-m200.html"
